<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>An empty 20-gallon water tank is filled at a constant rate for 3 minutes until it is half full. Then, it is emptied at a constant rate for 3 minutes.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph 3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>A full 10-gallon water tank is drained for 30 seconds, until it is half full. Afterwards, it gets refilled.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph 1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>A 2,000-gallon water tank starts out empty. It is being filled for 5 hours, slowly at first, and faster later.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph 2</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>An empty 100-gallon water tank is filled in 50 minutes. Then, a dog jumps in and splashes around for 10 minutes, letting 7 gallons of water out. The tank is refilled afterwards.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>Graph 4</para>
<para>For #6-7, use this situation and function:</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>The daily cost to the manufacturing company is modeled by the function </para>
  <para>\(C(x)=7.25x+2500\) where \(C(x)\) is the total daily cost and \(x\) is the number of items manufactured.</para>
</blockquote>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> What value equals \(C(0)\)?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 2500 </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>What does \(C(0)\) mean in the context of the situation?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>Cost before any items are manufactured</para></section>
